# ─── RICHBAYY CLIENT ENVIRONMENT ───────────────────────────────
# Copy to `.env` (or `.env.local`). In development you can leave VITE_API_URL
# unset — Vite proxies /api to http://localhost:5000 (see vite.config.js).
#
# For production (Vercel), point this at your deployed backend (Render):
# VITE_API_URL=https://richbayy-api.onrender.com/api
VITE_API_URL=/api

# ─── Firebase Phone Auth (customer sign-in) ────────────────────
# From: Firebase console → Project settings → General → Your apps → Web app.
# These values are PUBLIC by design (they identify the project, they don't grant
# access) — restrict the API key by HTTP referrer in the Google Cloud console.
# The matching service-account key lives on the SERVER only.
#
# Leave VITE_FB_API_KEY blank to fall back to the in-house OTP flow, which works
# out of the box in development (the code is logged by the API server).
VITE_FB_API_KEY=
VITE_FB_AUTH_DOMAIN=your-project.firebaseapp.com
VITE_FB_PROJECT_ID=your-project
VITE_FB_APP_ID=1:000000000000:web:0000000000000000000000
